# Data licence — read this before reusing anything in derived/

**This repository does not and cannot license the data it derives.**

The rest of the wss fleet publishes `derived/` under CC-BY-4.0. This repository
is the exception, and the exception is not a technicality.

## What the source says

`wdpa.protected.areas` captures the World Database on Protected Areas from
protectedplanet.net. UNEP-WCMC's terms
(<https://www.protectedplanet.net/en/legal>) say, verbatim:

> **No Sub-licensing or Redistribution of WDPCA and GD-PAME Data** — The WDPCA
> and GD-PAME Materials may not be sub-licensed in whole or in part **including
> within Derivative Works** without the prior written permission of UNEP-WCMC.
> You may not redistribute the WDPCA and GD-PAME Data contained in the WDPCA
> and GD-PAME in whole or in part.

and, on publishing:

> You may publish the WDPCA and GD-PAME Materials in whole or in part,
> including on-line, providing (a) the WDPCA and GD-PAME Data **are not
> downloadable** and (b) the proper attribution is clearly visible.

Two consequences, and neither is avoidable by wording:

1. **Applying CC-BY to `derived/` would be sub-licensing**, which the terms
   prohibit without written permission. This file used to carry the CC-BY text.
   That was wrong and it has been removed.
2. **A downloadable `derived/observations/*.csv.gz` is downloadable Data.** It
   holds 1,558,769 per-site observations across 312,943 protected areas. That
   is the attribute database, restructured — not an aggregate about it.

## What this means in practice

| | status |
| --- | --- |
| `examples/charts/*.svg`, `README.md` | **publishable.** Published, not downloadable, attributed. This is what the terms explicitly allow |
| aggregate rows — `feed:`, `country:`, `realm:`, `iucn:`, `status:` | ~1,300 rows of counts and totals. Defensible as statistics about the data rather than the data |
| `derived/observations/*.csv.gz` as a whole | **not publishable** while it contains the 1,558,769 `pa:` rows |
| `raw/` | never in git regardless; object storage only |

